the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the Jahreseinkommen of *a case* is *a number*; scenario element.
    the Unterlagen vollständig of *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Förderantrag holds for *a case*.
    Einkommensgrenze holds for *a case*.
    Dokumentenprüfung holds for *a case*.
    Einkommensgrenze would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r4_10_funding_application includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/funding-application.ruml".

Förderantrag holds for a case if
    Einkommensgrenze holds for the case
    and Dokumentenprüfung holds for the case.

Einkommensgrenze holds for a case if
    the Jahreseinkommen of the case is a number N
    and N < 50000.

% Where the expression has no result (a value it needs is missing), RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Einkommensgrenze holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the Jahreseinkommen of the case is a number
    and Einkommensgrenze would hold for the case.

Dokumentenprüfung holds for a case if
    the Unterlagen vollständig of the case is true.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "funding-application.ruml" at generated_1:
    % every data point its first value
    the Jahreseinkommen of case 1 is 50000.
    the Unterlagen vollständig of case 1 is true.
    node_1 expects answers [].
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Förderantrag holds for case 1"].
    node_2 expects answers [].
    not_node_2 expects answers ["it is not the case that Einkommensgrenze holds for case 1"].
    node_3 expects answers ["Dokumentenprüfung holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_3 expects answers [].

